 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=2 (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + H(+) + NADPH = 2diphosphate + NADP(+) + squalene; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:32295,ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:15440, ChEBI:CHEBI:33019,ChEBI:CHEBI:57783, ChEBI:CHEBI:58349, ChEBI:CHEBI:175763;EC=2.5.1.21;CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=2 (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + H(+) + NADH = 2diphosphate + NAD(+) + squalene; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:32299,ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:15440, ChEBI:CHEBI:33019,ChEBI:CHEBI:57540, ChEBI:CHEBI:57945, ChEBI:CHEBI:175763;EC=2.5.1.21;COFACTOR:Name=Mg(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:18420;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:24531458};PATHWAY: Terpene metabolism; lanosterol biosynthesis; lanosterolfrom farnesyl diphosphate: step 1/3.SUBUNIT: Monomer. {ECO:0000250}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Endoplasmic reticulum membrane; Multi-passmembrane protein.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=5;Name=1;IsoId=P37268-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=P37268-2; Sequence=VSP_056283;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;Name=3;IsoId=P37268-3; Sequence=VSP_056282;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;Name=4;IsoId=P37268-4; Sequence=VSP_056517;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;Name=5;IsoId=P37268-5; Sequence=VSP_056518;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Widely expressed.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:29909962}.DISEASE: Squalene synthase deficiency (SQSD) [MIM:618156]: Anautosomal recessive disorder characterized by profounddevelopmental delay, brain abnormalities, 2/3 syndactyly of thetoes, facial dysmorphisms, low total and LDL-cholesterol, andabnormal urine organic acids. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:29909962}.Note=The disease is caused by mutations affecting the generepresented in this entry.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the phytoene/squalene synthase family.{ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
